    "preflight": "ADDITIVE MANUFACTURING STUDIO\n\nPrint Lab\n\nShape a model, understand its physical scale and material tradeoffs, and prepare evidence for a staff-reviewed print request. Nothing here spends points or starts a printer.\n\n1. Design\n2. Preflight\n3. Materials\n4. Submit\nSchool printer profile\n\nUse the receiving printer’s actual build area. These values are not machine settings.\n\nBed width (mm)\nBed depth (mm)\nBuild height (mm)\nPlanning clearance (mm)\nNozzle diameter (mm)\n\nPlanning clearance is a conservative advisory buffer removed from both sides of each profile dimension. Adjust it for clips, purge lines, and local procedures; it is not a machine setting.\n\nGeometry World scale fits this profile\n\nModel envelope: 20 × 30 × 40 mm. Printer profile: 220 × 180 × 250 mm.\n\nIncludes the preferred 5 mm planning clearance. Profile changes update this check immediately; slicer and staff review remain required.\n\nRun advisory preflight\nAnalyze & Repair\n\nSTL repair only welds near-identical vertices and removes degenerate triangles. It does not fill holes, boolean-union shells, remesh, test wall thickness, or certify safety.\n\nCreate conservative repair candidate\nPreflight report\nPASS\nWIDTH\n20 mm\nDEPTH\n30 mm\nHEIGHT\n40 mm\nTRIANGLES\n104\n\nNo blocking condition was found by these limited checks.\n\nAdvisory, not certification. Print Lab does not prove wall thickness, self-intersection repair, support success, material suitability, or machine safety. A trained staff member must inspect the sliced result before accepting a request.\nPreflight completed without a blocking geometry error. Staff and slicer review are still required.\nSelected build prepared locally. Opening Print Lab.",
